# Problem solution `.c++` standard (gold: folder `01-Contains-Duplicate-…`)

Use **01-Contains-Duplicate-Arrays-Hashing-Easy** as the template for comment layout, naming, and style.

## Required header block (every approach file)

```text
Problem: <Name>
Link:    <leetcode url>

Approach: Brute Force | Optimized (…) | Optimal (…)

Idea:
<one short paragraph>

Steps (example <…>):
1. …

Time Complexity:  O(…) — <why>
Space Complexity: O(…) — <why>

Edge Cases:
- …

Example: <input> → <output>

Note: <optional>
```

## Code conventions

- 4 spaces; `class Solution {` / `public:` / `int main()` with `return 0;`
- Prefer `int` indices + `(int)nums.size()` (same style as prep pack)
- Prefer `unordered_set` / `unordered_map` with `.count(key)` (portable; matches prep sheets)
- Keep a small local `main` that prints one example — logic stays inside `Solution`
- Approach ladder must stay honest: Brute may be slow; Optimized mid; Optimal best practical here

## Sibling flowcharts

When this `.c++` file is created or its control flow changes, Cursor updates the matching `*.flowchart.md` (see `solution-flowcharts` rule). Never draw.io / png.
